{"availability":"available","full":"pramodganar/pmsm-temperature-prediction","name":"pmsm-temperature-prediction","description":"Regression model predicting PMSM permanent-magnet temperature from sensor readings, with leakage-safe session splitting, a shared inference pipeline, CLI, Flask API, and Streamlit app.","category":"Education","language":"Jupyter Notebook","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-07-07T07:13:04Z","updated":"2026-07-10T06:37:50Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://pmsm-temperature-prediction-dmtwdmtp9stfq6kyg84vh8.streamlit.app/","topics":["flask","gradient-boosting","machine-learning","pmsm","regression","scikit-learn","streamlit","time-series"],"demo":"https://pmsm-temperature-prediction-dmtwdmtp9stfq6kyg84vh8.streamlit.app/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T02:45:58.821Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T02:45:58.821Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T02:45:58.821Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T09:07:37.743Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-16T02:45:58.821Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Regression project to predict the permanent magnet tooth temperature (pm) of a permanent magnet synchronous motor (PMSM) from electrical and thermal sensor readings recorded across many driving cycles.","Because consecutive rows within a session are nearly identical, a random train/test split would scatter near-duplicate neighbours across both sides and report a falsely optimistic score. Holding out whole sessions is what makes the test set a fair measure of performance on a motor run the model has not seen. The random forest makes this concrete: it fits the training rows almost perfectly but generalises worse than linear regression to unseen sessions."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/pramodganar/pmsm-temperature-prediction/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"01b9a7255bb792ccde6aacc36e4e6eec22f902e7013e09443b371876d5e916e1","extract